#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Expert card-by-card GIH win-rate predictions for Reality Fracture (FRA).

Each entry: name -> (predicted GIH WR in %, short rationale).
Numbers are set after reading every card in the set, the FRA comprehensive
rules (empower Jace / prepare / behold), the SOS (Strixhaven predecessor)
17lands results, and historical analog cards across the 10 prior sets.

Context assumptions baked into the numbers
------------------------------------------
* Target set-wide mean card GIH WR ~ 55.8% (historical range 55.6-56.2%).
* Jace tokens: Empower N ~ N/3 cards of value (−3 draw) but delayed one
  activation per turn and vulnerable to attacks; also switches on all
  "if you control a planeswalker" payoffs (Commons/Annex duals, Way of ...,
  Sanctum Lurker, Mind Meanderer, Compel Brutality mode 2, Kiora, Avatar).
* Prepared creatures are built-in 2-for-1s (body now + spell later); they
  historically over-performed their stats in SOS.
* Common removal is plentiful (Memory Trap, Last Gasp, Extended Absence,
  Silence the Echo, Awaken the Inferno, No Admittance, Wrath of the Bloodmane,
  Infinite Coursework, Icy Reception, Compel Brutality) so cheap durable
  value and card advantage are at a premium; fragile x/1s are penalised.
* Five allied Elder Sphinx factions (WU scry/surveil, UB threshold/self-mill,
  BR noncombat damage/Cadets, RG Heartwood artifacts, GW counters/lifegain)
  plus enemy-pair legendary uncommons; a dedicated legendary slot (#195-280)
  means many narrow build-around legends will be played in decks that do not
  support them, which pulls their GIH WR toward/below average.
"""

